<p>The British anthem has seven descendants and the revolutionary anthems of France and Poland three each; the songs that reached furthest, from Scotland to Japan and Korea, from Poland to Spain, from Johannesburg to New York, did so through printed songbooks, translations and records. A few of the 32 links rest on weak ground, as the notes say. Even so, the pattern holds: tunes travel further than words, anthems breed anthems, and the children often outlive their parents in use.</p>
